      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This also occasionally causes hold interactions in the tools menu to fail and act as if I clicked the option instead.\n\nWhich is pretty important considering a chatbox hold menu has quick access to quickly clear a message you just wrote.\n\nBut with this bug.. it treats my action as a click causing a chatbox to open instead.. Which causes a message you might have wanted to clear sooner to instead stay up for about 3-4 extra seconds per failure, as you close a chatbox and open a menu again to attempt and do a hold interaction again..\n\nIt's inconsistent but seems to be more frequent at lower or inconsistent framerate.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-09-27T01:39:36.968Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While the new patch fixes clicks being outright dropped, I've noticed many times that actions are \"doubled\" instead now. For example, in the action menu, i will try to go into tools and it'll instantly jump to camera. Happens for all other UI elements as well. Another example, for the quick menu, I will open the worlds tab then it'll instantly double click and pull up some random world.\n\nI've tried using other mice, and friends have been having similar issues who are also on 1917, and did not have the issue on earlier builds.",
